 Workarounds
 ===========
 
+KK_WORKAROUND_17
+----------------
+| macOS version: 27.0
+| Metal ticket: Not reported
+| Metal ticket status:
+| CTS test failure: ``dEQP-VK.robustness.robustness2.bind.notemplate.rgba32i.unroll.volatile.storage_buffer.readonly.no_fmt_qual.len_16.samples_1.1d.comp``
+| Comments:
+
+A compute kernel that reads ``device`` memory through a ``coherent`` pointer
+inside a loop miscompiles: the first such load in an iteration returns the
+right value and every later one returns zero. Two coherent loads are enough
+and one is not, and any unrelated edit - storing a value as soon as it is
+produced, or changing the loop bounds - moves the failure to a different
+kernel rather than removing it, which is the same shape as
+KK_WORKAROUND_15. ``coherent(device)`` and ``volatile coherent`` reproduce it
+too.
+
+An application reaches this without asking for coherency, because glslang
+decorates a ``volatile`` buffer member ``Coherent`` as well as ``Volatile``.
+A robust read of a ``volatile`` storage buffer is one bounds-checked load per
+component, so a vec4 element comes back as its first component followed by
+zeroes and the shader sees neither the stored data nor the zeroes that an
+out-of-bounds read owes it.
+
+Perform a coherent 32-bit global access with ``atomic_load_explicit`` and
+``atomic_store_explicit`` under ``memory_order_relaxed``, one component at a
+time, instead of dereferencing a ``coherent device`` pointer. A relaxed device
+atomic is coherent at device scope by definition and the compiler cannot fold
+it away. Components with no MSL atomic type, and the accesses the driver marks
+coherent itself (KK_WORKAROUND_6), keep the pointer qualifier. Only a shader
+that has such an access declares the two helpers, so every other shader still
+translates byte for byte as before. Disabling this workaround restores the
+pointer qualifier for application coherency as well.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-09-12: Workaround implemented
+
 KK_WORKAROUND_16
 ----------------
 | macOS version: 26.x
